  <h1>Boiler Fails Its Service — What Happens Next (And Will I Get Charged More on the Day?)</h1>
  <p>This is the question underneath a lot of the hesitation we hear before a service even gets booked. People aren't worried about the £120. They're worried about what happens if the engineer finds something, and whether that turns into a much bigger bill they didn't see coming while they're standing in their own hallway. So let's deal with it directly.</p>

  <h2>What "failing" a service actually means</h2>
  <p>A boiler service isn't pass or fail in the way an MOT is. There's no certificate that says "failed" on it. What happens is more specific: during the checks, the engineer finds something that isn't right — a safety device not firing properly, a part that's worn beyond a safe tolerance, signs of corrosion inside the casing, that sort of thing. Most of the time it's one component, not the whole boiler, and most of the time it's something we've seen a hundred times before.</p>

  <h2>Will I get charged more on the day?</h2>
  <p>Not without you agreeing to it first. The £120 covers the full <a href="/boiler-servicing/">boiler service York</a> homeowners book with us — every check on the list, not a shortened version of it. If something needs fixing beyond that, we'll tell you exactly what it is, what it costs to put right, and why it matters, before any extra work happens. You can say yes, say you want to think about it, or say no. Nobody's signing anything on the doorstep under pressure. Only a small fraction of the people who call us ever mention price as their main concern, and we think that's because people trust they'll be told the truth rather than upsold — so that's what we stick to.</p>

  <h2>What usually causes a boiler to "fail" like this</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>A worn safety device.</strong> These are designed to shut the boiler down if something's wrong, and like any mechanical part they can wear out and need replacing on their own schedule.</li>
    <li><strong>Pressure that's drifted low or unstable.</strong> Sometimes it's a simple top-up, sometimes it points to a small leak worth tracking down properly.</li>
    <li><strong>A dirty heat exchanger.</strong> Build-up inside the part that actually heats your water is one of the most common things we find, and the main reason an annual <a href="/advice-centre/whats-included-boiler-service/">boiler service</a> exists in the first place.</li>
    <li><strong>A blocked condensate pipe.</strong> Easy to miss, and a common cause of a boiler cutting out in cold weather.</li>
    <li><strong>General age and wear.</strong> On an older boiler, parts fail simply because they've done their job for a long time. That's not a defect we're trying to sell you, it's just how appliances work.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Is it safe to keep using the boiler while I decide?</h2>
  <p>Depends entirely on what's been found. If there's any risk around carbon monoxide or gas safety, we'll say so clearly and won't leave a boiler running in that state — that's not negotiable, whatever you'd prefer to do. For most other issues, like a worn part that isn't an immediate safety risk, it's usually fine to keep using the boiler for a short while as normal, while you decide whether to go ahead with the repair there and then or get a second opinion. We'd rather you felt able to take a day to think it over than feel rushed into a decision.</p>

  <h2>Why we work this way</h2>
  <p>We've had plenty of customers tell us they've been let down by someone before, usually a quote that quietly grew once the job started. It's the fastest way to lose a customer for good, and it's not how we want to be known in York after eighteen years in this trade. If you're already on one of our <a href="/boiler-care-plans/">Care Plans</a>, the service itself is covered as part of your plan, and any genuine repair gets handled under whatever parts and labour cover your plan includes, so there's even less to weigh up on the day.</p>

  <h2>Booking a service you can trust</h2>
  <p>If you've been putting off booking an <a href="/advice-centre/do-i-need-annual-service/">annual boiler service York</a> warranty terms and your own peace of mind both depend on, purely because you're not sure what you'll be told on the day, give us a ring on <a href={siteConfig.phoneHref}>{siteConfig.phoneDisplay}</a> or WhatsApp <a href={`https://wa.me/${siteConfig.whatsappNumberIntl}`}>{siteConfig.whatsappDisplay}</a> and ask us how we handle it. We're happy to talk it through before you book, not just after.</p>
